8lop|v|A flat tablet or ledge of any material set horizontally at a distance from the floor, to hold objects of use or ornament. ; A sand bank in the sea, or a rock, or ledge of rocks, rendering the water shallow, and dangerous to ships. ; A stratum lying in a very even manner; a flat, projecting layer of rock. ; A piece of timber running the whole length of a vessel inside the timberheads.	o:3so5,90,3;1179,82,6;58w3,77,2321;3ixz,72,14;5phy,68,5;59sh,68,33;11c7,61,4;3ixe,59,4;2469,51,3;1pkj,50,4;a8of,46,7;1h6e,42,20;1f6y,35,11;3z1p,29,60;1sx7,28,13~58w3,77,2321;8u78,17,261;8w4r,13,105;3z1p,29,60;a2m7,17,51;7b8f,5,42;59sh,68,33;2dun,0,25;5clh,1,21;1h6e,42,20;58gb,8,14;93s9,7,14;3ixz,72,14;1sx7,28,13;2yqu,23,11	s:5phy,93,28;5pb6,87,4;1179,84,7;5jna,84,4;6vgw,79,8;4zqv,74,6;9v9g,62,5;82m,59,3;11cj,56,3;a94j,53,6;8lrt,47,4;3gvd,46,6;3h46,45,11;6sdu,40,13;3v9e,39,3~5dtw,35,199;7h2z,31,175;2hyj,22,57;aqwv,13,37;5phy,93,28;58gd,0,25;a5gj,11,16;93s9,8,15;6sdu,40,13;3h46,45,11;6vgw,79,8;1179,84,7;4zqv,74,6;a94j,53,6;3gvd,46,6	D:8utu,17,33~8utu,17,33
