8loy|v|To strip or break off the shell of; to take out of the shell, pod, etc.; as, to shell nuts or pease; to shell oysters. ; To separate the kernels of (an ear of Indian corn, wheat, oats, etc.) from the cob, ear, or husk. ; To throw shells or bombs upon or into; to bombard; as, to shell a town. ; To fall off, as a shell, crust, etc. ; To cast the shell, or exterior covering; to fall out of the pod or husk; as, nuts shell in falling. ; To be disengaged from the ear or husk; as, wheat or rye shells in reaping.	o:1ory,56,2;5r4x,52,1;5r4w,40,10;8d2q,36,1;1w9o,35,10;1odf,34,2;3ozb,34,4;8jk4,34,4;3rim,30,5;8d0t,30,2;1xkd,29,3;8d0n,29,5;1ot9,27,923;7i1d,25,2;15k5,25,12~8d0v,5,1220;1ot9,27,923;8d56,19,352;34c9,12,135;4hqz,1,45;7th6,5,21;15k5,25,12;5r4w,40,10;1w9o,35,10;33fb,5,9;8d0n,29,5;alfb,9,5;3rim,30,5;4hr6,2,4;1vn2,7,4	s:7gvz,108,19;5goz,60,2;afg2,60,29;4o6y,56,2;9p2d,46,2;gr1,42,4;8wmt,41,2;3s5l,39,466;5xrp,38,1;4t41,36,1;51bb,35,1;51ds,34,4;8xoe,32,1;12a8,31,11;6av2,31,15~akfc,17,2107;3s5l,39,466;42o,30,202;4snj,22,100;a2tj,8,88;7an9,5,46;afg2,60,29;7abz,7,25;3tt2,6,25;5xpo,4,20;7gvz,108,19;6av2,31,15;12a8,31,11;9a12,27,10;9wto,20,7	d:f16,84,8;12a7,48,1;737s,48,4;6xvp,29,2;870g,26,10;3s5l,21,136;7l34,19,1;5riv,14,1;12a8,12,3;42o,8,46~3s5l,21,136;42o,8,46;870g,26,10;f16,84,8;737s,48,4;12a8,12,3;6xvp,29,2;12a7,48,1;7l34,19,1;5riv,14,1	D:2jt2,36,13;3ozb,14,1;8mg5,10,2;1tm8,2,4~2jt2,36,13;1tm8,2,4;8mg5,10,2;3ozb,14,1
