8mf7|n|One of the small pieces, or splinters, into which a brittle thing is broken by sudden violence; -- generally used in the plural. ; A thin slice; a shive. ; A variety of blue slate. ; A sheave or small wheel in a pulley. ; A small wedge, as for fastening the bolt of a window shutter. ; A spindle. ; The act of shivering or trembling.	a:75l8,116,5;1n86,79,16;4m9i,78,1;ai6u,47,4;8s1h,20,3~1n86,79,16;75l8,116,5;ai6u,47,4;8s1h,20,3;4m9i,78,1	v:1n86,49,2~1n86,49,2	V:7pbz,64,15;86qo,11,4~7pbz,64,15;86qo,11,4	n:4m9i,88,2~4m9i,88,2	N:aixo,32,2;86qo,11,4~86qo,11,4;aixo,32,2
